          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data. It performs static analysis only here: **no code is run**. We examined 3 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:3, File = c(\"fn_helpers.R\", \"fn_main.R\", \n\"tests/testthat/test-helpers.R\"), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"fn_helpers.R\", \n\"—\"), Basis = c(\"none\", \"dependency\", \"none\")), row.names = c(NA, \n-3L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Missing inputs",
          "Every data file the code reads is either produced by an earlier script or present in the repository.",
          "#### Files not run on their own",
          "1 file only defines functions, so running it on its own says nothing: a function counts when a script uses it. These files are not counted as scripts. 0 are used by no script in the deposit.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"fn_helpers.R\", \"Used by\" = \"fn_main.R, tests/testthat/test-helpers.R\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "1 file is not part of the analysis but of software (a package, its tests or documentation, a tool, a web application), so it was not run or counted as scripts.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"tests/testthat/test-helpers.R\", Why = \"It is a test of a package or the file that installs it, not part of the analysis.\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
